# Line-ending policy — mirrors the core repo's .gitattributes, which already solved this.
#
# Without this file, core.autocrlf=true on a Windows checkout makes every file a tool writes as LF
# show as "modified" (48 such phantom changes had accumulated on 2026-09-14, all byte-identical
# once line endings were normalised) and hides the one real change among them. It also breaks what
# ships: packages are deployed into a Linux container, a CRLF .sh dies there with
# `$'': command not found`, and the LF-exact install recipe's sha256 check against the blob
# fails on a CRLF working copy. Every text blob in this repo is already LF, so this changes no
# stored content — it makes the working copy agree with it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Force LF on everything a Linux shell or container executes or parses.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
.githooks/** text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalise. text=auto would already skip most of these, but an ASCII STL can
# be classified as text, and silently rewriting a geometry file's bytes is not acceptable.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.stl   binary
*.glb   binary
*.gltf  binary
*.bin   binary
*.wav   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.onnx  binary
*.npz   binary
*.db    binary
*.sqlite binary

# COLLABORATE.md is the shared multi-bot coordination thread (append-only). A union merge lets
# concurrent appends from different sessions auto-merge instead of conflicting — each session
# appends self-contained entries at the end. Same rule as the core repo.
COLLABORATE.md merge=union
